{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Six days you shall work, and on the seventh day you shall cease.</b> He mentioned the commandment of Sabbath in the middle of the festivals, for He placed it adjacent to the festival of matzot and to the sanctity of the firstborn, because in all of them there is a remembrance of the work of Creation. And it says, בחריש ובקציר תשבות — 'in plowing and in harvest you shall cease' — that is, even at the time of plowing and harvest, which are the core of human life in the cultivation of the land, you shall cease on the day of Sabbath and do no work in it. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:57.670709951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}